Section: Flying a mission
  On: desktop
  In AUTO, ArduPlane flies the items of the mission in order. After the last item, it
  decides where to go. It also decides when the mission starts again from the first item.

Vocabulary:
  Phrase: the plane is flying a short mission
    Say: do the steps of [[From plan to flight]], but plan only a takeoff and two waypoints, with no return. Click the waypoints at least 150 m apart and from home, because ArduPlane counts a waypoint as reached 90 m short of it. The VTOL lifts off by itself from the takeoff
    Given the plan has 3 items
    And the takeoff is planned
    And the last plan item is WAYPOINT
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    And the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is AUTO
    And the plane is flying the mission
    And the vehicle's current item is 1

Background:
  Follows: the console is connected to a plane on the ground
  Given the plane is flying a short mission
